[15:57:33] I rated NetApp (NTAP) AVOID at conviction 3, so no buy. The scorecard total was 7, below the buy bar, and the checker passed.

research/NTAP/2026-11-15-evaluation.md
OK research/NTAP/2026-11-15-evaluation.md Bear case=145 Bull case=139 decision=AVOID scorecard=7->3

- **For:** the business is strong. It has net cash, high returns, and operating margin and ROCE at two-year highs. The stock is up 62.6% over 12 months and 17.7% above its 200-day average.
- **Against:** the price is stretched. Its P/E, EV/EBITDA and P/FCF are all above their own 5-year highs. The price assumes 25.5% revenue growth next year. The mechanical base fair value is 87.50 against a close of 181.37.
- **FCF margin:** it fell over the last year, from 25.2% to 22.3%. I judged this temporary, because the 10-Q puts it down to memory and component costs that price rises are offsetting.
- **Entry price:** 70.00 (base fair value × 0.8). A close at or below it triggers a fresh review, not an automatic buy.
- **Next results:** Q2 results come out on 2026-12-01.

I rated the key risk "high": a de-rating if AI-storage growth slows. That rating cost the most points and was a judgement call. "Medium" would have added one point, total 8, still under the buy bar of 9. My scenario prices (240 / 165 / 106) are my own estimates, and the probability-weighted value is below today's price. The 10-Q gives no revenue split by country, so the macro overlay couldn't check country risk.
